---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Legal and correction process" description="Copyright, privacy, safety, provenance, correction, and legal complaint process for streisandeffect.org.">
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal and corrections</p>
    <h1>Takedown, correction, and context requests</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      streisandeffect.org reviews credible copyright, privacy, safety, provenance, factual, contextual, defamation, and other legal complaints.
    </p>
  </section>

  <aside class="notice warning" aria-label="Legal and correction scope">
    <strong>About this page</strong>
    <p>This page explains how to send a correction or takedown request. It does not determine anyone’s legal rights or the outcome of a request.</p>
  </aside>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Request categories</h2>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li><strong>Copyright:</strong> claims about ownership, licensing, infringement, or replacement copies.</li>
      <li><strong>Privacy and safety:</strong> requests involving personal information, doxxing, risk of harm, or sensitive data.</li>
      <li><strong>Provenance correction:</strong> source, date, chain-of-custody, file metadata, or checksum corrections.</li>
      <li><strong>Factual or contextual correction:</strong> missing context, misleading summaries, or disputed descriptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Defamation or other legal complaint:</strong> legal claims not covered above.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What to include</h2>
    <p>Send enough information for human review:</p>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>Your name and organization, if applicable.</li>
      <li>The exact streisandeffect.org URL at issue.</li>
      <li>The exact file, metadata field, or statement you are challenging.</li>
      <li>The request category.</li>
      <li>Evidence supporting the request.</li>
      <li>The specific action requested: correction, added context, temporary disabling, removal, or replacement.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:legal@streisandeffect.org">legal@streisandeffect.org</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>How requests are considered</h2>
    <p>Requests are more useful when they identify the specific page, file, or statement at issue and include supporting information. The archive may consider provenance, privacy, safety, factual context, copyright, and other relevant concerns when responding.</p>
    <p>A request does not itself establish that material will be changed, removed, or kept available.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Current public record</h2>
    <p>This site does not currently publish a public log of requests or historical record revisions. Current record pages show the metadata and checksum associated with the copy presented there.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
